    "narrative": "Our daily outlook for LawDog is led by **Lawrence Butler**, who provides the highest utility today with a 61.99 score despite a difficult matchup against Sonny Gray. His valuation is buoyed by a significant +10% park factor adjustment and a favorable +13% platoon edge against the right-hander, which more than compensates for the volatility of batting in the eighth spot. Similarly, **Cal Raleigh** remains a high-end start at 60.61; while his platoon splits against Roki Sasaki are suboptimal, the projected wind blowing out provides a crucial boost to his HR potential, keeping him well clear of our marginal-start threshold.\n\nConversely, our bench decision-making centered on **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 36.72 score. While he holds intriguing upside, the combination of a daunting matchup against Weathers\u2014carrying a 3.41 xERA\u2014and his suboptimal position in the order suppressed his efficiency below our 40-point floor. Meanwhile, the lineup is heavily dependent on favorable outcomes from **Jonathan Aranda** and **Luis Arraez**, both of whom see positive adjustments for their proximity to the top of the order, despite facing pitchers in the 3.50\u20134.30 xERA range.\n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding today's \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Cal Raleigh**, **Luis Arraez**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Drew Gilbert**. Any unexpected shift downward in the batting order for **Jung Hoo Lee** or **Drew Gilbert**\u2014both already sitting in the mid-40s\u2014would necessitate a re-evaluation of their starts to preserve our daily game caps. We are also monitoring the continued absence of **Bryce Harper** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** due to schedule gaps, along with the ongoing IL status of **Will Smith**, which limits our defensive flexibility and forces heavier reliance on the current active pool.",
